      "text": "This is somewhat unusual question. What I believe is asking \"what is every integer's multiple?\"\n\nMultiples are defined for integers\n\ndistinct integer a, b\nintegral m, n\nm(a) = b(m = (a/b) *n)\n\nEach multiple is also true for m = 1.\n\nMore generally multiple is:\n\nmA = all numbers of the form b(m = (1/b) *n)\n\nwhere n is bounded by n(b)  \n\nn = b(a - 1) \n& n(b+1)\n\nLet non zero b\n\nMultiple = sum - difference all n (b) by 1\nmultiple = (n(b+1) = 1(b-a+1) ) / (int)\n\nNo other method of end difficulty.",
